finding: Medium — src/standard/rendering/forward.ts:1504-1515: the warm flag is not reset at each StandardRenderingPlugin.warm start. It is reset only inside prepareStandardRenderer (1316), after warmPrepassTextures, warmClusters and the awaited warmLightCull have already run. After a successful warm, a re-warm leaves the flag true throughout those operations; if any throws/rejects, it stays true despite the failed warm, and preparePipelines still enters native preparation rather than taking the not-warm path. warmLightCull itself reallocates buffers, replaces pipeline state and awaits warmLightRaster (cluster.ts:1590-1622), so this is a real partially-reprepared state, not an empty preamble. Move the reset to the owning warm hook's entry and cover a failure before prepareStandardRenderer. The new tests exercise initialize-time and successful late loads only, so they do not detect this failure.
